TI  - A 44-year-old man with hemoptysis.
PG  - 343-347
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_282_17 [doi]
AB  - A 44-year-old man with background history of diffuse cutaneous systemic sclerosis 
      and dilated cardiomyopathy receiving immunosuppressive medications, presented 
      with a 2-month history of cough and streaky hemoptysis. Clinicoradiological 
      features were consistent with an endotracheal mass. Subsequently, the patient 
      developed nodular skin lesions and the tracheal mass increased in size causing 
      central airway obstruction. This clinicopathologic conference discusses the 
      clinical and radiological differential diagnoses of such a clinical presentation 
      and their management options.
