TI  - Tracheobronchomalacia and excessive dynamic airway collapse.
PG  - 388-406
AB  - Tracheobronchomalacia and excessive dynamic airway collapse are two separate 
      forms of dynamic central airway obstruction that may or may not coexist. These 
      entities are increasingly recognized as asthma and COPD imitators. The 
      understanding of these disease processes, however, has been compromised over the 
      years because of uncertainties regarding their definitions, pathogenesis and 
      aetiology. To date, there is no standardized classification, diagnosis or 
      management algorithm. In this article we comprehensively review the aetiology, 
      morphopathology, physiology, diagnosis and treatment of these entities.
