TI  - Central Airway Obstruction Due to Tracheal Glomus Tumor.
PG  - e43-e45
LID - 10.1055/s-0038-1675411 [doi]
AB  - Background  Tracheal glomus tumors are rare mesenchymal neoplasms that have the 
      potential to cause malignant, central airway obstruction. They require a 
      thoughtful approach to safely secure the airway and definitively resect the 
      tumor. Case Description  We report the clinical course of a 25-year-old man in 
      severe respiratory distress secondary to tracheal glomus tumor and the subsequent 
      surgical management. Conclusion  Due to their hypervascular nature, greater 
      familiarity with tracheal glomus tumors is needed to ensure appropriate 
      preoperative planning and intervention.
