DP  - 2023 Mar
TI  - Airway and Hemodynamic Considerations for the Anesthetic Management of an 
      Intraluminal Tracheal Plasmacytoma.
PG  - 64-67
LID - 10.1177/10892532221140235 [doi]
AB  - Central airway obstruction due to tracheal tumors presents unique challenges to 
      the anesthesiologist. We present the case of a 44-year-old male taken to the OR 
      for biopsy and resection of an undiagnosed tracheal mass. Intraoperative 
      management was complicated by bleeding and significant hemodynamic instability, 
      necessitating rapid surgical and anesthetic intervention. This ultimately led to 
      abortion of surgical resection. Pathologic examination revealed a primary 
      tracheal plasmacytoma, a rare type of tracheal tumor. Here, we describe 
      anesthetic and hemodynamic considerations for a tracheal plasmacytoma. We discuss 
      the approach to airway management in variable intrathoracic tracheal obstruction 
      and the unpredictability of tracheal tumors.
