TI  - Endobronchial chondroid hamartoma of left main bronchus and its bronchoscopic 
      management.
PG  - 282-284
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_547_22 [doi]
AB  - Most tumours of the tracheobronchial tree are malignant. Benign tumours such as 
      hamartoma are infrequent and generally intra-parenchymal. Here we present a case 
      of a 65-year-old male patient who presented with a purely endobronchial lobulated 
      mass lesion in the left main bronchus. This central airway obstruction was 
      managed by a complete endobronchial resection using an electrocautery snare and 
      cryo-recanalisation techniques. A diagnosis of endobronchial chondroid hamartoma 
      was made on histopathological examination. Such endobronchial lesions are rare 
      and constitute less than 2% of all hamartomas.
