TI  - Carinal Compression from Primary Mediastinal Germ Cell Tumor.
PG  - e29227
LID - 10.7759/cureus.29227 [doi]
LID - e29227
AB  - Mediastinal masses can present as a medical emergency when there is central 
      airway obstruction, superior vena cava (SVC) syndrome, direct mediastinal 
      extension of tumor, or obstruction of the central pulmonary 
      vasculature. Diagnostic evaluation may include the need for invasive tissue 
      biopsy under anesthesia, which can pose several distinct risks for 
      patients. Among the many etiologies of mediastinal tumors, primary mediastinal 
      germ cell tumors are a rare form with a favorable prognosis.
