TI  - Central airway obstruction caused by adenoid cystic carcinoma in pregnancy: a 
      case report and review of the literature.
PG  - e00317
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.317 [doi]
LID - e00317
AB  - Malignancy complicates one in a thousand pregnancies. The most frequently 
      diagnosed of these are breast, cervical, melanoma, ovarian, and haematological 
      neoplasms. Tumours of respiratory origin are very uncommon during pregnancy. We 
      present a case of tracheal adenoid cystic carcinoma (ACC), a rare type of primary 
      airway tumour, diagnosed in a pregnant woman. To our knowledge, this is the third 
      reported case of tracheal ACC complicating pregnancy. We discuss potential 
      barriers to timely diagnosis of malignancies during pregnancy and consider 
      optimal management strategies, taking into account the potential harm to the 
      mother and foetus in a field with a limited evidence base.
