TI  - Temporary airway stenting for giant anterior mediastinal tumor biopsy: Two case 
      reports.
PG  - 157-160
LID - S2210-2612(19)30550-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ijscr.2019.10.005 [doi]
AB  - INTRODUCTION: When the management of an anterior mediastinal tumor requires 
      general anesthesia, airway narrowing and obstruction may occur secondary to 
      muscle relaxation. PRESENTATION OF CASES: Two men (ages, 15 and 36 years) 
      presented with a giant anterior mediastinal tumor and central airway obstruction. 
      We used Dumon stents to effectively secure the airway in both patients. After 
      chemotherapy, stent removal was safely performed in each case because the tumor 
      was substantially smaller. DISCUSSION: Dumon stents effectively secured the 
      airway. These stents were easily removed after chemotherapy without severe 
      complications. CONCLUSION: Temporary stenting is useful in patients with a giant 
      anterior mediastinal tumor who require general anesthesia.
