DP  - 2019 Sep-Oct
TI  - An Open-label, Single-arm Study of CRYO2 for Debulking at the Site of Central 
      Airway Obstruction or Stenosis.
PG  - 1641-1644
LID - 10.21873/invivo.11649 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: An open-label, single-arm study was conducted to assess the safety of 
      a cryosurgery unit named CRYO2 for debulking at the site of obstruction or 
      stenosis. PATIENTS AND METHODS: In order to treat central airway tumor-related 
      stenosis, debulking at the stenotic site of the airway was performed using CRYO2 
      under general or local anesthesia. The primary endpoint was the incidence of 
      moderate to massive hemorrhage. RESULTS: Incidence of moderate to massive 
      hemorrhage during surgery was 3.8% (1/26) (95% confidence 
      interval(CI)=0.1-19.6%). Technical success was 96.2% (25/26), with a 95% 
      confidence interval of 80.4-99.9%. CONCLUSION: CRYO2 for debulking at the site of 
      obstruction or stenosis can be performed safely.
