TI  - Malignant extra renal rhabdoid tumour presenting as central airway obstruction.
PG  - 950869
LID - 10.1155/2014/950869 [doi]
LID - 950869
AB  - Rhabdoid tumours are one of the most aggressive childhood neoplasms associated 
      with high mortality. The commonest age group affected is children less than five 
      years of age. Rhabdoid tumour presenting as an endoluminal tracheal mass leading 
      to central airway obstruction has not been previously reported. We describe the 
      case of a 17-year-old male patient where malignant rhabdoid tumour masqueraded as 
      bronchial asthma leading to a delayed diagnosis of upper airway obstruction by 
      tracheal growth. Histopathological examination and immunohistochemistry confirmed 
      the diagnosis of malignant rhabdoid tumour.
