TI  - Self-Expectoration of Airway Stent Following Chemoimmunotherapy in Extensive 
      Disease Small Cell Lung Cancer.
PG  - e70225
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70225 [doi]
LID - e70225
AB  - A 76-year-old man with extensive disease small cell lung cancer underwent airway 
      stenting for right bronchus intermedius stenosis. The stent self-expectorated 
      after initiating chemoimmunotherapy due to tumour shrinkage. Clinicians should be 
      aware of the possibility of stent migration in malignant central airway 
      obstruction patients who respond to chemotherapy.
