DP  - 2011 Jul
TI  - Cracking the case of foreign body aspiration.
PG  - 290-1
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3182238374 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspiration, although a leading cause of unintentional deaths in 
      children, is relatively uncommon in adults. The typical objects are food 
      particles, which are aspirated in patients with altered mental status or 
      pharyngeal dysfunction. We report an atypical case of foreign body aspiration in 
      an adult presenting with dyspnea and pleuritic chest pain. The patient was found 
      to have central airway obstruction secondary to an aspirated crack vial in his 
      left mainstem bronchus, requiring urgent rigid bronchoscopic removal.
